# Set the collision bitmask on every collision of a link (or of every link in
# the model when link is empty). Two collisions interact only when the bitwise
# AND of their masks is non-zero; the default is 0xFFFF.
#
# Used to stop a grasped object and the gripper fingers from colliding: the
# object gets 0x0001, the finger links get 0xFFFE. Both still collide with
# everything else (0xFFFF & either is non-zero), just not with each other.
string model
string link
uint32 bitmask
---
bool ok
string message
uint32 collisions_changed
